  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Menstrual health for deaf women in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to communication barriers, deaf girls and women in Zimbabwe are excluded from mainstream information on menstrual health. Consequently, some deaf girls and women resort to using materials, such as old t-shirts or newspapers during their mensuration, sometimes leading to an infection.  This project plans to train deaf girls to manufacture and then distribute sanitary packs and educate other deaf women on menstrual hygiene and improve the health outcomes of 80 deaf women in Manicaland.</narrative>
  </description>
